WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:07.515
Start with an empty project and a brief: a battery tray, removable electronics
bridge, and fixed mounting patterns.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:16.129
Codex builds the tray around the battery, adding mounting pads, strap guides and
side rails.

00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:17.804
The source stays editable.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:26.898
Codex adds the electronics bridge and assembles both parts.

00:00:26.898 --> 00:00:30.282
The frame and board mounting patterns match the brief.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:41.245
The baseline passes: zero point seven five millimeters of clearance per side.

00:00:41.245 --> 00:00:44.063
The checker measures the exported geometry.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:52.896
Now the battery requirement changes from thirty-five to forty millimeters.

00:00:52.896 --> 00:00:55.561
First, test it against the unchanged tray.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.313
The battery overlaps both rails.

00:01:01.313 --> 00:01:07.851
Clearance is minus one point seven five millimeters per side, and Codex preserves
the failed check.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:16.258
Codex widens the cavity to forty-one point five millimeters.

00:01:16.258 --> 00:01:22.075
Clearance returns to zero point seven five per side; the mounting patterns stay
fixed.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:33.741
With the bridge installed and straps removed, the battery’s insertion path clears.

00:01:33.741 --> 00:01:37.795
Codex packages the checked CAD, drawing and editable source.

00:01:37.795 --> 00:01:41.715
Rebuilding that source returns the same measured geometry.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:52.997
Now let’s build it in Codex, from the brief to the checked handoff.
